# Rank 1820 / CVE-2022-3215 (GHSA-7fj7-39wj-c64f): SwiftNIO's HTTP/1.1
# encoder wrote outbound header fields to the wire verbatim. writeHead in
# Sources/NIOHTTP1/HTTPEncoder.swift did `buffer.write(headers: headers)` and
# nothing anywhere in the pipeline policed the bytes, so a field value carrying
# CR or LF terminated the header block early and injected a second message:
# response splitting toward the browser (CWE-113), request smuggling against
# the upstream (CWE-444). The advisory's shape is not the NIOSSL certificate
# one -- the change diff is entirely in NIOHTTP1.
#
# Fix a16e2f54 adds NIOHTTPRequestHeadersValidator and
# NIOHTTPResponseHeadersValidator, channel handlers that reject a field name
# or value containing CR, LF, NUL or any other ASCII control character (HTAB
# allowed) per RFC 9110, installs them in configureHTTPServerPipeline and
# addHTTPClientHandlers with the switch defaulting to on, and compiles the
# llhttp C target with LLHTTP_STRICT_MODE for the inbound side. The commit
# message documents the opt-out: "For projects that are running the
# validation themselves, this can be easily disabled."
#
# The binding widens code.HttpHeaderValidationDisabled to Swift, the shape
# VYQL-INJ-247 judges for Netty's validateHeaders(false) on the Java
# side. Nothing is tainted and there is no path to trace -- the weakness is a
# control switched off at configuration, the same shape
# code.CertValidationDisabled occupies for TLS. The pre-fix tree has no
# switch to pass at all (the control did not exist), so no binding can fire
# on it; the durable, documentation-answerable fact the fixed revision introduces is the
# switch itself, and a consumer passing false re-creates this CVE's condition
# exactly -- the fixed revision's own regression tests assert that with
# withOutboundHeaderValidation: false a value containing \r reaches the wire
# byte for byte, Tests/NIOHTTP1Tests/HTTPHeaderValidationTests.swift:540 and
# :516, which are the shapes the cases below are modelled on.
#
# Swift appends a call's argument labels to the call node's path as dotted
# segments (swift.go, call_expression: `path += "." + strings.Join(labels,
// ".")`), so `callee.path ~= "withOutboundHeaderValidation"` holds exactly
# when that labelled argument is passed, whatever the receiver and whatever
# precedes it. That label is what does the discriminating, not the false
# literal's position: configureHTTPServerPipeline also takes
# withPipeliningAssistance and withErrorHandling booleans, and a false passed
# to either of those with validation left at its default is the test file's
# own line 495, pinned as a reject case below. The residual, documented in
# the binding, is a call that passes false to one of those and a computed
# value to the validation label itself.
#
# Engine gap, closed alongside: the real code's opt-out calls are whole
# statements headed by `try`, and swift.go's statement switch had no case
# for try_expression or await_expression -- its default returned nil, so
# `try f(x)` at statement position produced no IR at all while the same
# statement without `try` lowered normally. Measured at the vulnerable revision: a
# FuncDef whose body is a single `try g(a: false)` extracted with an empty
# body; the same call in return or assignment position carries a label. The
# minimal pair is the first expect case against the third one: the same
# statement with and without the `try` keyword, one reported and one not.
# The frontend now lowers a statement-position try/await through its
# operand's own statement handling, so the idiom is visible to every
# binding, not just this one.
#
# Measured bounded (timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB, --cache off), counts the
# union of three runs per revision, run from inside the worktree. swift-nio
# at a16e2f54^: 351 findings, 0 VYQL-INJ-247 -- the parameter does not exist
# at that revision, in Sources or Tests. At a16e2f54: 353 findings, exactly
# 2 VYQL-INJ-247, the disable-path regression tests at
# Tests/NIOHTTP1Tests/HTTPHeaderValidationTests.swift:516 and :540, and none
# anywhere under Sources/, where every call passes the defaulted or computed
# value. The whole delta between revisions is those two rows. Collateral of
# the frontend fix, measured as full finding-set diffs: swift-nio +2
# VYQL-LIFE-001 on real `self._lock.lock()` calls inside `try await` blocks
# (NIOAsyncWriter.swift:467, NIOThrowingAsyncSequenceProducer.swift:437),
# identical at both revisions; swift-crypto +8 VYQL-CRY-001 on real
# `Insecure.SHA1` constructions under Tests/; swift-corelibs-foundation
# 2744 -> 2744 and starscream 0 -> 0, no movement. Across the other Swift
# trees under /tmp/cve-work/rank*/ (swift-crypto-fixed, swift-asn1) the
# high-and-above counts are unchanged; grep finds the two argument labels
# only in this repository's own tests.

test "rank1820: a server pipeline configured with outbound header validation switched off"
  lang swift
  file Tests/NIOHTTP1Tests/ServerPipelineSetup.swift
  expect VYQL-INJ-247
  code
  ```
  import NIOCore
  import NIOHTTP1

  final class ServerPipelineSetup {
      let channel: EmbeddedChannel

      init() {
          self.channel = EmbeddedChannel()
      }

      func disableValidation() throws {
          channel.pipeline.syncOperations.configureHTTPServerPipeline(withErrorHandling: false, withOutboundHeaderValidation: false)
          channel.primeForResponse()
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1820: a client pipeline configured with outbound header validation switched off"
  lang swift
  file Tests/NIOHTTP1Tests/ClientPipelineSetup.swift
  expect VYQL-INJ-247
  code
  ```
  import NIOCore
  import NIOHTTP1

  final class ClientPipelineSetup {
      let channel: EmbeddedChannel

      init() {
          self.channel = EmbeddedChannel()
      }

      func disableValidation() throws {
          channel.pipeline.syncOperations.addHTTPClientHandlers(enableOutboundHeaderValidation: false)
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1820: the same server opt-out written as a whole try statement, the form the fixed revision's own regression test uses"
  lang swift
  file Tests/NIOHTTP1Tests/ServerPipelineSetupTry.swift
  expect VYQL-INJ-247
  code
  ```
  import NIOCore
  import NIOHTTP1

  final class ServerPipelineSetupTry {
      let channel: EmbeddedChannel

      init() {
          self.channel = EmbeddedChannel()
      }

      func disableValidation() throws {
          try channel.pipeline.syncOperations.configureHTTPServerPipeline(withErrorHandling: false, withOutboundHeaderValidation: false)
          try channel.primeForResponse()
      }
  }
  ```

